# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Placeholders only in this file — never commit
# a real value here. Next.js loads .env.local from this directory, which is why
# this template lives in fitos/ rather than the repository root; db/reset.sh and
# the psql scripts read the same PG* variables from the shell.

# --- Postgres connection -----------------------------------------------------
# The application connects as a role WITHOUT BYPASSRLS. Migrations and seeding
# run as a separate service role. See db/reset.sh.
PGHOST=127.0.0.1
PGPORT=5432
PGUSER=replace-with-app-role
PGPASSWORD=replace-with-password
PGDATABASE=replace-with-database-name

# --- Identity hashing peppers ------------------------------------------------
# HMAC keys for contact hashing. Two separate keys on purpose:
#
#   FITOS_ORG_HASH_SECRET   derives a per-organization key, so two retailers
#                           holding the same person produce different hashes and
#                           the platform cannot correlate customers across
#                           retailers as a side effect of the schema.
#   FITOS_IDENTITY_SECRET   the global key behind identity_lookup_hash.
#
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 48
# Rotating either one invalidates every hash derived from it. Never log these.
FITOS_ORG_HASH_SECRET=replace-with-random-48-byte-base64-value
FITOS_IDENTITY_SECRET=replace-with-a-different-random-48-byte-base64-value
